From 6137be9beb327ebd85ae869c55641f1cd89d984d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 05:27:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ci): preserve the upstream image suite deadline

Restore the medium-suite timeout for large image fixtures after queue
patch 0013 shortens generated unit suites to 60 seconds. Keep all 13 tests
and their existing assertions. Add an analysis regression for the timeout.

Base: rust-v0.163.0 (83086188ae0614bd882818ff1aa23f3194962012)
with the maintained queue through 0074.
Red: native Intel macOS run 39099539998/job 117592792112 reports
Expected "moderate", but got "short" for whole_suite_deadline_test.
Earlier full and normal/serial native runs exceed the 60-second deadline.
The unchanged complete payload passes all 13 tests with upstream's
300-second budget in the same native job (25.10 seconds).
Green: the maintained run-bazel-ci.sh test entry point passes the unchanged
regression with --strategy=TestRunner=local --nocache_test_results.
Local Linux sandbox device errors require this existing local-runner
strategy; the clean rerun retains Codex's outer sandbox.
Maintained just fmt-check and just bazel-lock-check pass.
Fresh emitted and full native configured execution remain required.
---
 codex-rs/utils/image/BUILD.bazel | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/codex-rs/utils/image/BUILD.bazel b/codex-rs/utils/image/BUILD.bazel
index 0bc9e6b17..6228ee13c 100644
--- a/codex-rs/utils/image/BUILD.bazel
+++ b/codex-rs/utils/image/BUILD.bazel
@@ -1,6 +1,16 @@
 load("//:defs.bzl", "codex_rust_crate")
+load("//tools/build-warnings/test-timeouts:timeouts_test.bzl", "timeout_test")
 
 codex_rust_crate(
     name = "image",
     crate_name = "codex_utils_image",
+    # Preserve the upstream medium-suite budget for large image fixtures.
+    unit_test_timeout = "moderate",
+)
+
+timeout_test(
+    name = "whole_suite_deadline_test",
+    size = "small",
+    expected_timeout = "moderate",
+    target_under_test = ":image-unit-tests",
 )
